                        <div id="accordions" class="accordion">
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse1"><span><strong>Q1:</strong> What types of books can be printed (paperback, hardcover, spiral-bound)?</span></div></div><div id="collapse1" class="collapse show"><div class="card-body text"><p>We print across all major binding formats, perfect-bound paperbacks, case-bound hardcovers with dust jackets or case laminate, spiral-bound and wire-bound books, saddle-stitched booklets, and coil-bound workbooks. The right binding depends on your book's purpose, page count, and how it'll be used. Novels and narrative non-fiction typically suit perfect-bound paperback or hardcover. Workbooks, cookbooks, and reference guides often benefit from spiral or wire binding that lets pages lie flat. We'll recommend the best option for your specific book during your consultation.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse2"><span><strong>Q2:</strong> Do you offer both short-run and bulk book printing services?</span></div></div><div id="collapse2" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>Yes. Short-run printing covers anything from a single proof copy to a few hundred units, ideal for author copies, local events, limited editions, or testing demand before committing to larger quantities. Bulk printing starts at around 500 copies and uses offset production methods that significantly reduce per-unit cost at higher volumes. We also offer print-on-demand, which eliminates minimum quantities entirely by printing each copy individually as orders come in. The right approach depends on your sales strategy, your budget, and whether you need physical inventory or prefer zero-stock distribution.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse3"><span><strong>Q3:</strong> What file format is required for printing my book?</span></div></div><div id="collapse3" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>Print-ready PDF is the standard file format for book printing. Your interior PDF needs to include correct trim marks, bleed settings, embedded fonts, and appropriate resolution for all images (300 DPI minimum). Your cover file needs to be a single PDF incorporating front cover, spine, and back cover at the correct dimensions for your page count and trim size. If you don't have print-ready files, we offer formatting and cover design services that produce files built to the exact specifications of your chosen printing method, so you don't need to learn pre-press production to get your book printed.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse4"><span><strong>Q4:</strong> Can you help with layout, design, and binding options?</span></div></div><div id="collapse4" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>Yes. We offer complete layout, interior formatting, cover design, and binding consultation as part of our publishing services. If your manuscript isn't print-ready yet, we can handle everything from interior typesetting and cover design through to final file production, delivering print-ready PDFs built to your chosen specifications. During your consultation, we'll walk through binding options, trim sizes, paper stocks, and cover finishes, recommending what works best for your genre, your audience, and your budget.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse5"><span><strong>Q5:</strong> How long does the book printing process take?</span></div></div><div id="collapse5" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>Turnaround depends on the printing method and quantity. Print-on-demand copies are typically produced and shipped within five to seven business days of an order being placed. Short-run digital printing takes seven to fourteen business days from file approval to delivery. Bulk offset runs take three to five weeks depending on quantity, binding complexity, and shipping logistics. Rush production is available for urgent deadlines, subject to availability. We'll give you a clear timeline during your consultation based on your specific project.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse6"><span><strong>Q6:</strong> What is the minimum order quantity for printing books?</span></div></div><div id="collapse6" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>There is no minimum. Print-on-demand allows you to print a single copy at a time with no upfront commitment. Short-run digital printing is economical from as few as ten or twenty copies. Bulk offset printing typically starts at around 500 copies, which is where per-unit costs drop significantly enough to justify the larger production run. We'll recommend the most cost-effective approach based on how many copies you need and what you're planning to do with them.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse7"><span><strong>Q7:</strong> Do you provide print-on-demand services?</span></div></div><div id="collapse7" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>Yes. We set up print-on-demand through Amazon KDP, IngramSpark, and other major providers, giving your book worldwide availability without any upfront printing costs or inventory risk. Each copy is printed individually when a customer places an order, shipped directly to the buyer, and you receive royalties on every sale. We handle file preparation, platform setup, and quality control to ensure your print-on-demand copies meet the same professional standards as traditionally printed books.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse8"><span><strong>Q8:</strong> What is the cost of book printing in Melbourne?</span></div></div><div id="collapse8" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>Printing costs vary based on format, page count, paper stock, colour or black-and-white interior, binding type, cover finish, and quantity. A standard black-and-white paperback novel is one of the most affordable formats to produce. Full-colour hardcovers, photo books, and illustrated children's books cost more due to premium materials and production complexity. Print-on-demand carries no upfront cost, you pay per copy as orders are placed. We quote every project individually based on your book's specific details, with no hidden setup fees or surprise charges.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse9"><span><strong>Q9:</strong> Can I request sample prints before final production?</span></div></div><div id="collapse9" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>Yes, and we strongly recommend it. Every print job includes a proof copy, a physical sample of your finished book produced exactly as it will appear in the final run. You review the proof for print quality, colour accuracy, paper feel, binding, and overall presentation before approving production. If anything needs adjusting, we make changes and produce a revised proof. We never commit to a full print run without your written approval of a physical proof you've held in your hands.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse10"><span><strong>Q10:</strong> Do you offer delivery or distribution after printing?</span></div></div><div id="collapse10" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>Yes. Finished books can be delivered to any address in Australia, your home, your office, an event venue, a bookshop, or directly to a distribution partner. For larger orders, we coordinate shipping logistics and can arrange warehousing if you need storage before distribution. Print-on-demand titles are shipped automatically to individual customers each time an order is placed, handled entirely by the platform. For authors who want broader retail distribution, we offer publishing services that place your book with distributors supplying bookshops, libraries, and online retailers across Australia and internationally.</p></div></div></div>
